### Padelteammates — parcours complet (REST Client VS Code / IntelliJ HTTP)
### Prerequis: docker compose up -d && npm run prisma:migrate && npm run seed && npm run dev

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@adminEmail = admin@padel-kenitra.ma
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123!

### 0. Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### --- ADMIN ---

### 1. Login admin (seed)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.token}}

### 2. Lister les clubs de Kenitra
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/clubs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3. (Admin) creer un club
# @name createClub
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/clubs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nouveau Club Padel", "city": "Kénitra" }

###
@clubId = {{createClub.response.body.id}}

### --- JOUEURS ---

### 4. Inscription joueur 1 (createur)
# @name reg1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Youssef", "email": "youssef@example.com", "password": "password123", "profilePublic": true }

###
@token1 = {{reg1.response.body.token}}
@user1 = {{reg1.response.body.user.id}}

### 5. Inscription joueur 2
# @name reg2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara", "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "password123", "profilePublic": true }

###
@token2 = {{reg2.response.body.token}}
@user2 = {{reg2.response.body.user.id}}

### 6. Inscription joueur 3
# @name reg3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mehdi", "email": "mehdi@example.com", "password": "password123" }

###
@token3 = {{reg3.response.body.token}}
@user3 = {{reg3.response.body.user.id}}

### 7. Inscription joueur 4
# @name reg4
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Amine", "email": "amine@example.com", "password": "password123" }

###
@token4 = {{reg4.response.body.token}}
@user4 = {{reg4.response.body.user.id}}

### --- PLANIFICATION ---

### 8. Joueur 1 cree un match et invite 2, 3, 4 (la date doit etre aujourd'hui ou dans le futur)
# @name createMatch
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clubId": "{{clubId}}",
  "date": "2026-09-20",
  "slot": "18:00-19:30",
  "creatorTeam": "A",
  "invites": [
    { "userId": "{{user2}}", "team": "A" },
    { "userId": "{{user3}}", "team": "B" },
    { "userId": "{{user4}}", "team": "B" }
  ]
}

###
@matchId = {{createMatch.response.body.id}}

### 9. Joueur 2 voit ses notifications (invitation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notifications?unread=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}

### 10. Joueurs 2, 3, 4 acceptent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/respond
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accept": true }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/respond
Authorization: Bearer {{token3}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accept": true }

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/respond
Authorization: Bearer {{token4}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accept": true }

### 11. Calendrier hebdomadaire (semaine du match)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/calendar/weekly?from=2026-09-20
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### --- SCORES ---
### Le resultat ne se saisit qu'a l'issue du creneau (heure de Kenitra). Pour tester tout de suite,
### deplacer le match a la veille (remplacer <matchId>) :
###   docker exec padel_postgres psql -U postgres -d padel_teamates -c "UPDATE \"Match\" SET date = CURRENT_DATE - 1 WHERE id = '<matchId>'"

### 12. Joueur 1 saisit le resultat (= validation de l'equipe A). Equipe A gagne 2-1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/score
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "teams": { "A": ["{{user1}}", "{{user2}}"], "B": ["{{user3}}", "{{user4}}"] },
  "games": [
    { "sets": [ { "a": 6, "b": 4 }, { "a": 6, "b": 3 } ] },
    { "sets": [ { "a": 2, "b": 6 }, { "a": 4, "b": 6 } ] },
    { "sets": [ { "a": 7, "b": 5 }, { "a": 3, "b": 6 }, { "a": 6, "b": 2 } ] }
  ]
}

### 13. Joueur 2 (coequipier) valide -> reste PENDING (awaitingTeams: ["B"]) : il faut un validateur par equipe
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/score/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}

### 14. Joueur 3 (equipe adverse) valide -> match COMPLETED + stats
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/score/validate
Authorization: Bearer {{token3}}

### 15. Stats publiques du joueur 1 (gagnant, profil public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{user1}}/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 16. Stats du joueur 3 (perdant, profil PRIVE -> 403 attendu)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{user3}}/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### --- COMPOSITION (sur un match encore planifie, creneau a venir) ---

### 17. Le joueur 3 quitte le match : sa place redevient libre
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/participants/{{user3}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token3}}

### 18. L'organisateur retire le joueur 4 (qui est notifie)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}/participants/{{user4}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 19. L'organisateur annule le match (204) : il disparait, les joueurs sont notifies
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/matches/{{matchId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}

### 17. Classement (profils publics)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/leaderboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token1}}
